  :adr/body
  "# ADR-2607195400: Browser worker SAB bridge for synchronous Kotoba HTTP imports

**Status**: accepted
**Date**: 2026-07-19

## Decision

Browser-hosted Kotoba WebAssembly executes in a dedicated worker. A synchronous
`http_get` guest import posts its capability-scoped request and a bounded
SharedArrayBuffer to the main thread, waits with Atomics, and receives at most
the guest-declared response capacity. The main thread performs the asynchronous
provider operation, writes only a Uint8Array within that capacity and notifies
the worker. Timeout, provider failure, malformed response and overflow all fail
closed.

The serving origin must enable cross-origin isolation with COOP and COEP. This
bridge does not grant browser fetch authority by itself: the existing host
capability grant, operation quota and endpoint policy remain authoritative.

## Maturity boundary

The executable evidence covers a real Chromium page, module worker, compiled
Wasm import and the SAB/Atomics bridge. It does not qualify Firefox or WebKit,
production headers/CDN behavior, redirect policy, PKI/revocation behavior or
long-duration soak reliability."}]
